---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Colophon - Karthik Gurumoorthy"
  description="How karthikg.in is made: Astro, Vercel, DigitalOcean DNS, and the identity files that make the site portable."
>
  <div class="section">
    <div class="container content">
      <h1>Colophon</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        How this site is put together. I write the words. Agents help with the
        making; I review what they produce.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>Site</h2>
        <p>
          A static site built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro 5</a> and
          TypeScript. Project entries are markdown in a content collection.
          There is no database, account system, or analytics.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Hosting and DNS</h2>
        <p>
          Production is the Vercel project
          <code>karthikg80s-projects/personal-site</code>, deploying from
          <code>main</code>. The <code>karthikg.in</code> zone stays on
          DigitalOcean. Only the apex <code>A</code> record points at Vercel
          (<code>76.76.21.21</code>). Nameservers were not moved, so mail,
          <code>supabase.karthikg.in</code>, and the studio subdomains stay put.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Identity</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Homepage <code>h-card</code> with name, URL, email, and org.</li>
          <li>
            <code>rel="me"</code> to
            <a href="https://github.com/karthikg80">GitHub</a>,
            <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/karthikg.in">Bluesky</a>,
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/karthikg80/">LinkedIn</a>, and
            <a href="https://theafoundry.com">Thea Foundry</a>.
          </li>
          <li>Project RSS at <a href="/rss.xml">/rss.xml</a>.</li>
          <li>
            AT Protocol handle <code>@karthikg.in</code>, proven by
            <a href="/.well-known/atproto-did"><code>/.well-known/atproto-did</code></a>
            and a <code>_atproto</code> DNS TXT record.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Source</h2>
        <p>
          The code is at
          <a href="https://github.com/karthikg80/personal-site">github.com/karthikg80/personal-site</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .content {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  section h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  section p,
  section li {
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  section ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  section li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
  }
</style>
